                                                                                                                <comments>
                            <comment id="14963892" author="sircodesalot" created="Mon, 19 Oct 2015 19:19:47 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Added patch (PR-283).&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="15047169" author="rdblue" created="Tue, 8 Dec 2015 18:08:47 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Merged PR #283. Thanks for fixing this, Reuben!&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16200597" author="arjun_kr" created="Wed, 11 Oct 2017 17:06:14 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=rdblue&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;rdblue&quot;&gt;rdblue&lt;/a&gt; Is it possible to make this fix available in parquet 1.8.1 as well ?  The fix is currently available in 1.9 and 1.8.2 . Apache Hive use parquet 1.8.1 and this issue is causing log flooding for parquet 1.6 files in Hive.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16200657" author="rdblue" created="Wed, 11 Oct 2017 17:43:42 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=arjun_kr&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;arjun_kr&quot;&gt;arjun_kr&lt;/a&gt;, releases are immutable, so we don&apos;t make changes to them. Since this is in the 1.8.2 release, I&apos;d recommend updating to that or asking your Hadoop vendor to make sure they backport this to their distribution.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="17857312" author="rok" created="Sun, 23 Jun 2024 03:27:38 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;This issue has been migrated to &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/apache/parquet-java/issues/1866&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;issue #1866&lt;/a&gt; on GitHub. Please see the &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/PARQUET-2502&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow&quot;&gt;migration documentation&lt;/a&gt; for further details.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
